WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.113
- This is my first time on television.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.560
- Oh, you mean not doing a Zoom?

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.393
- Yeah.

00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:07.226
- Oh wow.

00:00:07.226 --> 00:00:09.400
- Yeah, this is my first in
studio, it's very exciting.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.722
Hi everybody!

00:00:10.722 --> 00:00:11.555
- You look so beautiful!

00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:12.388
- Thanks!

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:13.221
- I mean, I need people to know

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:14.490
that even when you're at her house

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.323
and you're having dinner,

00:00:15.323 --> 00:00:20.275
even in her simple clothes,
you feel less than.

00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:21.696
(audience laughter)

00:00:21.696 --> 00:00:22.784
- You're crazy!

00:00:22.784 --> 00:00:24.586
- You're like, "Is that
what God intended?"

00:00:24.586 --> 00:00:26.330
- No, oh my goodness.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.330
Just sitting down, I've been
doing this crazy EMS workout,

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.847
electro muscle stimulation,

00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:36.480
and my whole butt hurts
so just sitting down.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.720
- Wait, does that mean
it works out for you?

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.640
- It's 20 minutes but it's like
working out for four hours.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.400
and you're hooked up to this moist wetsuit

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.030
with electronic stuff
stuck to your muscles,

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.380
and then you do little
movements through it,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.350
and then we're all just dying.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.940
All my hair and makeup people, everybody.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.013
We're all dead.

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:00.116
- Everybody sees your body and right now,

00:01:00.116 --> 00:01:00.949
(Chrissy laughs)

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:01.782
I think the internet is gonna crash

00:01:01.782 --> 00:01:04.400
because everyone is racing to get this.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.233
- No, no.

00:01:05.233 --> 00:01:06.580
I'm actually gaining weight through out

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.170
and I'm like, "Oh,
that's just muscle right?

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.516
Yeah, it's for sure muscle.

00:01:09.516 --> 00:01:10.349
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:10.349 --> 00:01:11.267
- That's what my friend
said, she was like,

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.437
"How am I working out and getting fatter?"

00:01:15.157 --> 00:01:16.270
- I think you get cocky
with food, that's why.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.830
- Ah, I just do that in general.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:19.739
(Chrissy laughs)

00:01:19.739 --> 00:01:22.770
So you and John spent the
Grammy nights dressed like this

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.820
which, this is amazing!

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.653
Look at you!

00:01:25.653 --> 00:01:27.186
- [Chrissy] We got bored.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.019
- [Kelly] Was that just in your closet?

00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:31.130
- We were so bored, I texted
one of my stylists, Monica

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.350
and I was like, "I feel so bad."

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.863
Because she had been asking
me for months if we were going

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:41.320
and then, I was under the
impression there was no Grammy's

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.440
and then you know what it's like

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.300
when your award isn't televised

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.660
and then you're like, "Oh
I probably didn't win,"

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:48.878
or whatever.

00:01:48.878 --> 00:01:49.711
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:49.711 --> 00:01:50.544
- And then they're like, "John
your award is televised!"

00:01:50.544 --> 00:01:51.850
And I was like, "You won!"

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.658
- Oh! (Kelly laughs)

00:01:54.658 --> 00:01:55.620
He did win!

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.886
- He won the un-televised one, yeah.

00:01:57.886 --> 00:01:59.211
(audience claps)

00:01:59.211 --> 00:02:00.887
- Yeah but whatever, it's
best R&amp;B album right?

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:01.720
- [Chrissy] I know!

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.553
- Yeah!

00:02:02.553 --> 00:02:03.980
- [Kelly] I have another photo though,

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.434
so I wanna ask you about what's happening-

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:07.267
- [Chrissy] Oh God! (laughs)

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.100
This went over well.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.287
- [Kelly] Did it not?

00:02:09.287 --> 00:02:10.830
(Chrissy laughs)

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.720
- I was backstage in your
beautiful dressing room,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.520
you have hands-down the best dressing room

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.403
of any talk show out there, always.

00:02:16.403 --> 00:02:17.236
- (gasps) Thank you! Thanks!

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.170
- This is even better, somehow.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:24.050
Okay so anyway, I've been
backstage just on my Twitter like

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:26.100
as my daily thing is threatening to quit

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.840
or threatening to deactivate,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.610
and then this one I was like,
"Oh Instagram's nice though!"

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.520
And then nope, they showed
me that they were upset.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.750
- What happened? What do you mean?

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.280
- We were trying to
take beauty glam photos

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.590
and he was just in the middle of it

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.170
but yeah people were really
bothered by it, I don't know.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:43.610
- My son's hilarious anytime
he walks in my bathroom

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.680
and I happen to be naked or something

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.570
and he's always like, "Naked baby!"

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.037
(Chrissy laughs)

00:02:49.037 --> 00:02:50.230
- Naked baby!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.920
- And I'm like, now I feel dirty about it.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.260
- My daughter, Luna's
always like, "Naked baby!"

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.780
- [Kelly] That's what my kids do!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:01.780
- And I mean, we take baths
together, I don't see the issue.

00:03:01.782 --> 00:03:02.810
- I think everybody's
comfort level is different

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.890
but here's my favorite part about any

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:05.830
of this social media stuff.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.178
I love that you clap back, and I love that

00:03:09.178 --> 00:03:12.160
the most interesting concept to me is,

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.900
why do people -

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.170
- follow you?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.003
- I know.

00:03:16.003 --> 00:03:16.836
- Follow you, If they don't like you

00:03:16.836 --> 00:03:18.494
or if they have a problem
with what you're doing?

00:03:18.494 --> 00:03:19.327
- [Chrissy] I know.

00:03:19.327 --> 00:03:22.007
- It is the most interesting thing to me,

00:03:22.007 --> 00:03:23.206
cause I don't have time!

00:03:23.206 --> 00:03:25.430
- Cause I have the time, I
do, and I'll go to their page,

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:29.170
and it's always they follow
me and their page is private,

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.720
without hesitation, every
time it's like that.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.553
- Wow!

00:03:32.553 --> 00:03:34.410
- But yeah, you cause you
think they'd know by now,

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.500
I haven't changed through all these years.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.333
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:39.680
- It's just yeah I think people -

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.120
- And your social media
account is supposed to be

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.170
a representation of who you
are, like this is who you are,

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.780
so like OK cool you don't like it?

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:45.613
Bye!

00:03:45.613 --> 00:03:47.153
- And what's really weird
is the psychology of it

00:03:47.153 --> 00:03:49.290
like really learning about people

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.810
because obviously we had a
really weird, rough year,

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.230
and then when people decide
that their pity for you is over,

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:00.230
and "Oh, it's noon and it's
time to be mean again,"

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.280
like, now it feels appropriate?

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.258
- Yeah.

00:04:03.258 --> 00:04:06.080
- It's such an odd, icky
thing to look at people doing

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.650
like it just felt like
honestly one weekend,

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.880
everyone was like, "Oh we don't
feel bad for them anymore,

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.790
and we're gonna do this."

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.194
- Wow.

00:04:14.194 --> 00:04:15.027
- I remember going through all of that,

00:04:15.027 --> 00:04:17.950
going through all the
emotion after a miscarriage,

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.977
or a stillborn, and
telling John that like,

00:04:20.977 --> 00:04:24.200
"Wow, the amount of love
we're getting both in person

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.270
and online is like, unheard of for me,

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.660
I'm not used to this!"

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.500
And then just one day, it was over.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.600
- Now that's just a sad statement!

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.908
- Yeah.

00:04:31.908 --> 00:04:32.741
- Yeah.

00:04:32.741 --> 00:04:35.266
- My big thing now is I just want to

00:04:35.266 --> 00:04:38.030
follow all the same people I
follow, maybe work with Twitter

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.985
but not allow anyone to follow me.

00:04:40.985 --> 00:04:41.951
- Oh.

00:04:41.951 --> 00:04:43.480
- And I don't want to ever
speak, but I want my same list-

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.363
- Yeah.

00:04:44.363 --> 00:04:45.635
- of people that I follow
because I genuinely,

00:04:45.635 --> 00:04:47.640
it's been 11, 12 years on Twitter now

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.060
so those are my buddies!

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:49.893
- Wow!

00:04:49.893 --> 00:04:50.726
That's a long time, I forgot.

00:04:50.726 --> 00:04:54.443
- Yeah, it's a long time
to take a constant beating.

00:04:54.443 --> 00:04:55.357
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:55.357 --> 00:04:57.240
- But you, (groans)

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.940
You would think it would
make you stronger, no!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.410
I think weakened me.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.780
- Do you go and I go
emotionally, like being

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.275
in the limelight in general,
I go like a roller coaster.

00:05:06.275 --> 00:05:07.108
- [Chrissy] Yeah.

00:05:07.108 --> 00:05:08.780
- Like not a severe one,
but kinda like a woo!

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.180
Cause some days I'm just
like, "I can handle anything!"

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.013
I'm like, whatever.

00:05:12.013 --> 00:05:13.710
And other days I'm like, "Why?"

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.220
- Some days I'm like, "I
have a beautiful family,

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.280
a perfect husband, like I
really have an incredible life."

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.113
- Blessed.

00:05:19.113 --> 00:05:19.946
- And some days I'm like,

00:05:19.946 --> 00:05:21.350
"I don't know if I can do this anymore-

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.261
- Yeah.

00:05:22.261 --> 00:05:24.320
- like this is overwhelming,
I don't know I can be on here

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.530
and interact with people
that want me to fail.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.514
- But that's what I like about you,

00:05:28.514 --> 00:05:29.347
you're not perfect online.

00:05:29.347 --> 00:05:30.180
That's what I like, and even in person,

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.232
like even us at dinner,
like you're not perfect,

00:05:32.232 --> 00:05:34.850
you're very normal and you're
very raw in the moment.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.900
I think that is so freaking refreshing,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.943
- Thank you.

00:05:37.943 --> 00:05:38.776
- 'cause I don't think
most people are like that.

00:05:38.776 --> 00:05:40.950
- It's hard to make mistakes
in front of everybody,

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:41.783
- Yeah.

00:05:41.783 --> 00:05:43.180
- for that many years.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.350
- But I love that you own it,
and you're like, "That's me!"

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:47.010
And then maybe you think it's a mistake,

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.650
like even if you do make
a mistake you apologize

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.770
but at the same time might
not be a mistake to you.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.410
You might be like, "Well
that's just who I am

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.603
or how I am."

00:05:54.603 --> 00:05:55.436
- Well tell that to my therapist

00:05:55.436 --> 00:05:56.410
because they are just like
itching for me to talk to them.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.410
- Well, why don't we trade?

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.145
You can talk to my therapist
and I'll talk to yours!

00:05:59.145 --> 00:06:00.820
(Chrissy and Kelly laugh)

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.901
- We'll probably have the
same issues, we're so similar.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.397
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.648
- [Kelly] I don't know I hope you don't.

00:06:05.648 --> 00:06:06.481
(audience cheers)

00:06:06.481 --> 00:06:08.135
- I wanna discuss a serious
topic with you as well,

00:06:08.135 --> 00:06:12.020
so, we're seeing protests
against anti-Asian violence,

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.430
and I just wanna know your thoughts on it.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:17.710
- It's actually what's been
happening has been incredible.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.100
A lot of people have
been reaching out to me

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.810
and wondering how they
can help, what they can do

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.880
and I love to post tangible
things that people can do

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:28.070
because there's all sorts
of performative activism.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:28.903
- Mm-hmm.

00:06:28.903 --> 00:06:32.778
- I think we just came out
of a long line of politicians

00:06:32.778 --> 00:06:36.340
that put a target on Asian people's backs

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.350
by calling it "the China virus,"

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:41.920
and so people are seeing Asian
people out on the street,

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.960
I automatically think of like
when my mom's without me,

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.793
how do people look at her?

00:06:45.793 --> 00:06:47.570
How do people treat her?

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:50.490
A lot of mothers and
fathers are being targeted

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:54.847
around the country and
it is so obvious to me

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.680
what the motive is, it
doesn't seem to be obvious

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.690
to the politicians out there

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.390
that are saying like, "We're
not quite sure of the motive."

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:07.610
But I think we know what it
is and if people can just

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.440
reach out in any way to support the

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:14.426
Asian-American community, AAPI in general,

00:07:14.426 --> 00:07:17.760
there's Stop AAPI Hate, which
is a wonderful organization

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:21.420
to donate to, and an organization
called 18 Million Rising

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.190
is really incredible, but
also it's little things

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.230
like supporting Asian-owned
businesses around you,

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.240
supporting your local Chinatown,

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.800
I mean these things are
disappearing quicker

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.765
than we know it and soon
they're gonna be gone

00:07:33.765 --> 00:07:36.890
and it's heartbreaking to me
so support any way you can.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.030
Don't just be the person
that reaches out via text

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:40.490
and checking in on you.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:41.740
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:43.710
- We all have to have
each others backs in this

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.010
because Asian Americans are Americans!

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:48.280
They came here for, my
mother came here for the

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.200
American dream, she
got to have a cookbook!

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.400
- My great grandfather did the same thing!

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.233
- Yeah!

00:07:53.233 --> 00:07:54.687
- We're all immigrants, we're
all from immigrants yeah.

00:07:54.687 --> 00:07:57.770
- And it's nobody's birth
right here that they are

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.120
the only ones to enjoy
the fruits of America,

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.590
that's just not a fact.

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.430
There is plenty for everybody

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:06.660
and we should welcome anyone
who wants to come here

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.620
to make their dreams possible, that's it.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.830
- Yeah, I think especially
having children it's so hard,

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:12.890
and your children!

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:15.250
- It's so odd because
they are so young still,

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:17.960
they're 2 and 4, Luna almost 3 and 5.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.760
- They will start picking
up though, especially Luna.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.330
- I know, and right now I
think what we talk about a lot

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.500
is representation,
representation in the media

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.600
and representation in Disney shows.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.780
Rya The Last Dragon was
incredible for us to see-

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:28.910
- I love Raya!

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:33.820
- on television, Luna's
like, "Uncle has a Tuk Tuk"

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.400
and "Oh, we eat rice
porridge in the morning"

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.500
and "She has hair like me!"

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.383
And you know it's just,

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.410
You know first hand, I'm sure,

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.983
that kids notice things so early,

00:08:45.983 --> 00:08:46.816
- Yeah.

00:08:46.816 --> 00:08:47.649
- they notice how they're unique-

00:08:47.649 --> 00:08:48.482
- Sponges!

00:08:48.482 --> 00:08:50.390
- and they notice their
differences and yeah and at school

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.570
and they just happen to
be more vocal about it

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:55.240
so it's important to explain it to them

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.660
in the simplest of ways
that they're different

00:08:58.660 --> 00:08:59.890
but they're beautiful, they're unique.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:04.700
But yeah, it's so crazy
to me that Luna can look

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:05.533
at a princess and be like,

00:09:05.533 --> 00:09:07.240
"Why don't I have blonde, straight hair?"

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.270
And I'm like, "It's different

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:10.037
but it's beautiful, don't worry!"

00:09:10.037 --> 00:09:12.790
- Yeah, alright so wait I
need to talk about this,

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.100
just sitting here this is awesome.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.070
We need to talk about your new
brand of cleaning products.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.160
- Yes!

